## 8. AI-Specific Requirements (Probabilistic Specs, Evals & Guardrails)
*Unlike deterministic software, AI systems require explicit tolerances, data contracts, autonomy boundaries, and failure UX.*

### 8.1 Data Supply Chain & Privacy
* **Data Sources & Provenance:** [Exact tables, docs, or APIs ingested].
* **Freshness & Sync Cadence:** [Real-time / 15-min / Daily / Weekly].
* **Tenant Isolation & Permissions:** [Enforce row-level security / RBAC so User A never retrieves Tenant B's vectors or documents].
* **Data Residency & Retention:** [Pin inference and storage to e.g. `us-east-1` or `eu-central-1`; enable Zero Data Retention (ZDR) on LLM APIs].

### 8.2 Model, Schema & Latency Budgets
* **Structured Output Contract:** [Enforce Pydantic / JSON Schema validation; 0% tolerance for malformed JSON].
* **Probabilistic Quality Thresholds (Measured on Golden Dataset):**
  * **Retrieval Recall@K / Groundedness:** $\ge$ [e.g., 90%] faithfulness to retrieved sources.
  * **Classification / Extraction Accuracy:** $\ge$ [e.g., 95%] recall on critical triggers.
* **Latency & Unit Economics Envelope:**
  * **Time to First Token (TTFT):** $<$ [e.g., 1.5 seconds] for interactive chat.
  * **End-to-End Pipeline Latency:** $<$ [e.g., 8 seconds] for agent loops.
  * **Cost Ceiling:** $<$ $[X] per 1,000 runs / $[Y] per tenant per month.

### 8.3 Agent Autonomy & Tool Permissions Matrix
*Define what the AI can do alone versus where it must pause.*

| Tool / Action | Side Effects | Reversibility | Autonomy Level | Guardrail / Approval Gate |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `search_docs` / `read_logs` | None (Read-only) | N/A | **Autonomous** | Scoped strictly to tenant ID |
| `draft_response` / `tag_record` | Writes internal metadata | Reversible | **Suggest Only** | Logged with confidence score |
| `post_public_reply` / `restart_service` | External / Production impact | Irreversible | **Escalate / HITL** | Mandatory human click-to-approve |

### 8.4 Evaluation Gate & Failure Modes (Fallback UX)
* **Golden Dataset & CI Gate:** [Minimum 30–50 curated test cases covering happy paths, multi-intent inputs, out-of-scope queries, and adversarial prompt injections; run automatically via Promptfoo/DeepEval before deployment].
* **Degraded State / Fallback UX:**
  * *Low Retrieval Confidence:* Do not guess—display *"I couldn't verify this in your documentation"* and offer 1-click escalation to a human.
  * *LLM Timeout / Rate Limit (429):* Retry with exponential backoff; fall back to secondary model or queue for async delivery.
  * *Loop Runaway:* Hard cap at `max_iterations = [5]` and token budget cap per run.

