## 9. Go-To-Market (GTM) Approach
*Plan how the product reaches users, drives adoption, and proves ROI post-launch.*

### Rollout Phases
1. **Phase 1 — Internal Dogfooding & Shadow Mode (Week 1):** Run the AI pipeline silently on live production data; compare AI tags/answers against human baselines without exposing outputs to end users.
2. **Phase 2 — Design Partner Beta (Weeks 2–3):** Onboard 3–5 friendly customers/operators; collect daily qualitative feedback and thumbs-up/down trace ratings.
3. **Phase 3 — General Availability (Week 4+):** Full rollout with in-app onboarding checklists, documentation, and ROI reporting.

### Packaging, Enablement & Success Tracking
* **Pricing / Packaging Tie-In:** [Included in core tier / Usage-based add-on / Enterprise tier differentiator].
* **Customer Onboarding & Enablement:** [1-page quickstart guide, sample prompts/alerts, and 90-second walkthrough video].
* **Post-Launch KPI Dashboard (30 / 60 / 90 Days):**
  * **Adoption:** Weekly Active Users (WAU) and % of alerts/digests opened.
  * **Quality:** Human override rate, thumbs-down rate, and live eval drift.
  * **Business Impact:** Measured reduction in manual hours, ticket deflection rate, or SLA recovery.

